Cell["Message functions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3e7d78be-027a-415a-b3bf-84710470c1da"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two observers ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " exchange light. The ",
 StyleBox["message relation",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " sends a tick ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to the ticks ",
 StyleBox["E", "TI"],
 "\:207a(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") \:2229 ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " on its light cone, and a ",
 StyleBox["message function",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a single-valued selection of it that preserves the order of the ticks, \
the discrete form of the Ehlers\[Dash]Pirani\[Dash]Schild axiom D1. An ",
 StyleBox["echo function",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a message function to ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " composed with one back to ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"edf66c08-a91e-402d-8cd1-72125c4b0b0a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The worldline ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " above (blue) and a longest chain ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " of the rest of the lattice (green), with the light rays that carry the \
messages from ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " (red)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"866bdaac-716f-4ba8-bc6a-15f40fcb30e8"],

